    <fr:title text="Compiling the Grammars Code">Compiling the Grammars Code</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>daily</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>We've been looking to <fr:link href="https://github.com/maxsnew/grammars-and-semantic-actions/issues/31" type="external">compile the cubical code used for Dependent Lambek Calculus</fr:link>, but it seems that it is infeasible to compile any non-erased cubical.</html:p>
    <html:p>This is especially problematic, because <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\epsilon ]]></fr:tex> and literals each are encoded with a path type. We may be able to find another strategy to encode them, but it would require moderate refactors. For example, the definition of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\epsilon ]]></fr:tex> uses a path type. But, we could define a version using the builtin (non-cubical) equality type. Or perhaps a version that pattern matches on the string.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
